The files in this directory come from three sources.

1. The MAME project (https://github.com/mamedev/mame), under the BSD-3-Clause
   licence below, taken from pico-galagino, which took them from
   pico-mooncresta:

     z80.c, z80.h                src/devices/cpu/z80/z80.cpp, z80.h, z80.inc
                                 Juergen Buchmueller; one addition,
                                 z80_hold_irq() (MAME's HOLD_LINE)
     z80.lst                     src/devices/cpu/z80/z80.lst, unchanged
                                 Juergen Buchmueller, Andrei I. Holub
     z80_ops.h                   generated from z80.lst by tools/z80gen.py,
                                 which is derived from src/devices/cpu/z80/
                                 z80make.py: Andre I. Holub

   The memory map, the inputs and the DIP switches of the board in
   dl_machine.c follow src/mame/cinematronics/dlair.cpp (Aaron Giles).

2. Hypseus Singe (https://github.com/DirtBagXon/hypseus-singe), a fork of
   DAPHNE, under the GNU General Public License version 2 or (at your option)
   any later version, used here under version 3:

     ldv1000.c, ldv1000.h        ported from src/ldp-in/ldv1000.cpp
                                 Copyright (C) 2001 Matt Ownby, with
                                 contributions by Mark Broadhead
     ldplayer.c (search, play    following src/ldp-out/ldp.cpp
     and pause rules)            Copyright (C) 2001 Matt Ownby

   The laserdisc strobe timing, the DIP switch defaults, the fast boot patch
   and the scoreboard layout in dl_machine.c follow src/game/lair.cpp
   (Copyright (C) 2001 Matt Ownby; Mark Broadhead, Robert DiNapoli, Jeff
   Kulczycki).

3. Original to pico-dragonslair, under the GNU General Public License v3.0
   with the rest of the project: ay8910.c/.h, dlair.h (with the parts named
   above), ldstream.c/.h, pld.c/.h, scoreboard.c/.h, dl_port.h, and
   romload.c/.h (adapted from pico-mooncresta).

